WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.970
The Saw franchise has become a complex saga
comprising many movies.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:09.490
And with the release of Spiral: From the Book
of Saw, things are about to get more complicated.

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:14.980
We're here to break down the entire Saw timeline,
one bloody moment at a time.

00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:19.739
John Kramer's sinister arc begins with his
time as an engineer and building designer.

00:00:19.739 --> 00:00:24.599
John works with his friend, attorney Art Blank,
on creating low-income housing for needy families

00:00:24.599 --> 00:00:26.510
through their Urban Renewal Group.

00:00:26.510 --> 00:00:29.919
Jill, John's wife, works at an addiction recovery
clinic.

00:00:29.919 --> 00:00:34.399
John is concerned over the safety of Jill's
workplace, especially as his wife is pregnant

00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:35.850
with their first child.

00:00:35.850 --> 00:00:40.420
His fears prove to be well-founded when a
patient named Cecil Adams attempts to rob

00:00:40.420 --> 00:00:41.420
the facility.

00:00:41.420 --> 00:00:46.050
Cecil shoves a heavy door into Jill's stomach
on the way out, causing her to miscarry the

00:00:46.050 --> 00:00:47.780
couple's unborn son Gideon.

00:00:47.780 --> 00:00:53.210
Cecil had been encouraged to go to the clinic
by Amanda Young, a fellow addict and patient

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:56.230
who was once arrested by Detective Eric Matthews.

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:59.910
John and Jill's relationship falls apart shortly
after this incident.

00:00:59.910 --> 00:01:04.920
A doll John had created for his unborn son
later inspires Jigsaw's ominous visage.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:09.960
Shortly after the decline of his marriage,
John is diagnosed with terminal cancer by

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:13.080
Dr. Lawrence Gordon of the Angel of Mercy
Hospital.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:16.310
During his treatment, John befriends an orderly
named Zep Hindle.

00:01:16.310 --> 00:01:19.020
Zep makes it clear that he dislikes Dr. Gordon.

00:01:19.020 --> 00:01:23.170
His tumor is deemed to be inoperable because
John was diagnosed too late, thanks to an

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:25.820
X-ray labeling error by Logan Nelson.

00:01:25.820 --> 00:01:31.020
John seeks approval for an alternative treatment
option with insurance executive William Easton,

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:34.360
a donor to Jill's clinic who is nevertheless
tightfisted.

00:01:34.360 --> 00:01:37.200
"And a new trial's starting.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:38.680
He's looking for new patients.

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:41.380
And he seems to think that I'm the perfect
candidate."

00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:45.750
John is warned he will lose his coverage with
Umbrella Health if he pursues experimental

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:50.090
treatment, as the company is quick to cut
off clients in need of care, like cardiac

00:01:50.090 --> 00:01:51.750
patient Harold Abbott.

00:01:51.750 --> 00:01:53.910
This decision comes back to haunt Easton.

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:57.920
None of these people know they've made a grave
mistake by simply being in the vicinity of

00:01:57.920 --> 00:02:02.410
John Kramer during this dark hour, but in
time, they definitely find out.

00:02:03.410 --> 00:02:07.670
After experiencing severe depression, John
drives himself off of a cliff.

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:12.230
But he survives the crash and gains a new
perspective on life, and an incessant urge

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:14.340
to force this revelation on others.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:19.060
He begins his deadly series of games with
a bit of retribution, concealing himself with

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:21.660
a pig mask and capturing Cecil.

00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:25.630
John places Cecil in restraints in his lab
and tells him that he has the choice to either

00:02:25.630 --> 00:02:30.350
bleed out from the wounds on his wrists, or
press his face through a series of blades.

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.990
John insists he'll escape with a renewed lease
on life.

00:02:32.990 --> 00:02:35.920
However, Cecil is unable to complete his challenge.

00:02:35.920 --> 00:02:38.970
But then, his chair breaks apart and allows
him to escape.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:43.800
Cecil attacks John, but John murders him by
throwing him into a cage full of razor wire.

00:02:44.800 --> 00:02:48.240
Jigsaw reveals Logan Nelson to have been John's
first sidekick.

00:02:48.240 --> 00:02:52.540
Logan fails to wake up during the initial
Bucket Head trap at Tuck's Pig Farm, and is

00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:54.660
badly wounded by the blades.

00:02:54.660 --> 00:02:59.709
But John does not believe Logan has to die
due to his careless-but-innocent X-ray mislabeling.

00:02:59.709 --> 00:03:04.130
John rescues Logan from the trap and trains
him in his philosophy, which Logan finds to

00:03:04.130 --> 00:03:05.130
be helpful.

00:03:05.130 --> 00:03:09.040
It is not clear how long Logan works with
John, but he helps him prepare some of his

00:03:09.040 --> 00:03:11.840
earliest traps, including the Reverse Beartrap.

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:16.330
We also don't know if he had any relationship
with Jigsaw's other sidekicks.

00:03:17.330 --> 00:03:19.630
Jigsaw's recruitment spree doesn't stop with
Logan.

00:03:19.630 --> 00:03:24.380
Mark Hoffman is part of the first Metropolitan
Police Department team investigating the Jigsaw

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:29.430
murders alongside Detectives David Tapp, Steven
Sing, and Allison Kerry.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:32.810
He learns enough about Jigsaw to imitate his
methods.

00:03:32.810 --> 00:03:37.620
Pretending to be Jigsaw, Hoffman gets vengeance
against Seth Baxter, his sister's murderer,

00:03:37.620 --> 00:03:39.360
via the Pendulum trap.

00:03:39.360 --> 00:03:43.180
Jigsaw does not punish Hoffman, though he
does admonish him for not giving Seth a chance

00:03:43.180 --> 00:03:44.560
to survive his trap.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:46.830
John offers to take him under his wing.

00:03:46.830 --> 00:03:50.930
Hoffman also helps John frame Dr. Gordon by
leaving the doctor's penlight at the scene

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:56.319
of Mark's game, after he warns John that Detective
Tapp is getting close to identifying him.

00:03:56.319 --> 00:04:00.390
Tapp narrowly survives a trap laid for the
police, but Sing is killed.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:03.140
Thus, Tapp's obsession with the case grows.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:07.680
John also recruits Amanda after she survives
her trap, and the three work together to create

00:04:07.680 --> 00:04:11.110
several traps, including one of the franchise's
most unforgettable.

00:04:12.349 --> 00:04:16.720
After Amanda agrees to become Jigsaw's second
protégé, she helps John orchestrate the

00:04:16.720 --> 00:04:18.519
infamous Bathroom trap.

00:04:18.519 --> 00:04:23.180
She helps kidnap Dr. Gordon, who is having
an affair with a student, and Adam Stanheight,

00:04:23.180 --> 00:04:27.090
who is photographing Gordon
for Detective Tapp.

00:04:27.090 --> 00:04:30.289
Amanda sets up the room so that Jigsaw can
play his sinister game.

00:04:30.289 --> 00:04:34.840
Gordon wins by sawing off his own foot, and
his wife and daughter also escape Zep with

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:35.840
Tapp's help.

00:04:35.840 --> 00:04:39.919
Gordon drags himself through the halls of
Jigsaw's lair and finds a hot steam pipe to

00:04:39.919 --> 00:04:41.740
cauterize his leg wound.

00:04:41.740 --> 00:04:46.669
Jigsaw then takes Gordon in to help him recover,
even devising a prosthetic for his leg.

00:04:46.669 --> 00:04:50.949
Amanda sneaks back into the bathroom to asphyxiate
Adam, who is already bleeding out.

00:04:50.949 --> 00:04:54.250
Gordon goes on to become Jigsaw's secret helping
hand.

00:04:54.250 --> 00:04:58.789
As revealed in Saw: The Final Chapter, he
assists with some of the more medically-sensitive

00:04:58.789 --> 00:05:03.809
tests, including the Venus Flytrap from Saw
II and the Mausoleum trap from Saw IV.

00:05:03.809 --> 00:05:07.719
He also suggests Lynn Denlon as a test subject
in Saw III.

00:05:07.719 --> 00:05:11.629
"I was his patient and he was mine."

00:05:12.629 --> 00:05:14.779
In Saw II, John is finally identified as the
Jigsaw killer.

00:05:14.779 --> 00:05:17.870
Eric Matthews is among the officers who finds
his hideout.

00:05:17.870 --> 00:05:22.349
Little does he know, John has kidnapped Matthews'
teenage son Daniel and put him into a group

00:05:22.349 --> 00:05:27.129
trap at the Nerve Gas House, alongside Amanda,
Addison, and several other people who'd been

00:05:27.129 --> 00:05:30.150
arrested by Matthews on bogus charges.

00:05:30.150 --> 00:05:34.559
After almost all of the subjects die, Daniel
is put into a safe with an oxygen mask and

00:05:34.559 --> 00:05:36.530
hidden in Jigsaw's lair.

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:40.910
Detectives Matthews, Kerry, and Daniel Rigg
arrive with others at Jigsaw's lair, and are

00:05:40.910 --> 00:05:44.819
unaware that the footage of the group trap
they are presented with was pre-taped.

00:05:44.819 --> 00:05:49.219
Instead of waiting like he is instructed to
do, Matthews brutalizes John and forces him

00:05:49.219 --> 00:05:51.770
to take him to the location of the trap.

00:05:51.770 --> 00:05:55.950
While Rigg discovers that the source of the
video feed is another empty house, Matthews

00:05:55.950 --> 00:06:01.029
ends up alone at the actual location, and
is captured and trapped by Amanda in the bathroom.

00:06:01.029 --> 00:06:05.439
In Saw III, it is revealed that Matthews breaks
his own foot to escape the shackle, but he

00:06:05.439 --> 00:06:07.310
is still captured for another game.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:11.289
Saw III takes place six months after Matthews
is captured.

00:06:11.289 --> 00:06:12.900
John Kramer is near death.

00:06:12.900 --> 00:06:16.319
He gives his lawyer a box containing instructions
for Jill.

00:06:16.319 --> 00:06:21.289
Meanwhile, Amanda is secretly resorting to
self-mutilation and creating unsurvivable

00:06:21.289 --> 00:06:23.710
traps, including one used on Kerry.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:28.250
John doesn't want to be replaced by a murderer,
and devises one last test for Amanda.

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:32.469
John has Amanda abduct Dr. Lynn Denlon and
put her into a neck trap.

00:06:32.469 --> 00:06:36.240
Denlon is forced to keep John alive for the
duration of another test, which turns out

00:06:36.240 --> 00:06:38.219
to involve her husband Jeff.

00:06:38.219 --> 00:06:42.389
Lynn and Jeff lost a son and have emotionally
neglected their daughter, who was kidnapped

00:06:42.389 --> 00:06:44.110
before Jeff's test.

00:06:44.110 --> 00:06:48.389
Little does Amanda know, her survival depends
on being able to let Denlon go.

00:06:48.389 --> 00:06:53.020
Hoffman slyly tells Amanda to kill Denlon,
threatening to expose her part in Cecil's

00:06:53.020 --> 00:06:55.729
attack on Jill's clinic if she refuses.

00:06:55.729 --> 00:06:58.969
Amanda refuses to let Denlon go and shoots
her instead.

00:06:58.969 --> 00:07:02.789
Jeff enters the room shortly thereafter and
kills Amanda in retaliation.

00:07:02.789 --> 00:07:08.210
For Jeff's final test, John asks him to show
mercy, but Jeff cuts his throat with an electric

00:07:08.210 --> 00:07:10.110
saw, triggering Denlon's collar.

00:07:11.110 --> 00:07:14.960
In Saw IV, it is revealed that Hoffman was
pretending to be trapped alongside the now-haggard

00:07:14.960 --> 00:07:19.069
Matthews and Art as the events in John's hospital
room unfolded.

00:07:19.069 --> 00:07:23.849
Rigg is confronted with several of Art's worst
clients, including Morgan, who just survived

00:07:23.849 --> 00:07:26.729
a test that forced her to kill her abusive
husband.

00:07:26.729 --> 00:07:31.210
Rigg is supposed to let his timer run out
but instead rushes into the final room with

00:07:31.210 --> 00:07:32.960
Hoffman, Matthews, and Art.

00:07:32.960 --> 00:07:36.969
Not knowing who's rushing in, Matthews shoots
Rigg and triggers a device that crushes his

00:07:36.969 --> 00:07:37.969
own head.

00:07:37.969 --> 00:07:41.809
Rigg also shoots Art, thinking the tape recorder
in his hand is a gun.

00:07:41.809 --> 00:07:46.229
Before Rigg bleeds out, he sees Hoffman reveal
himself as Jigsaw's apprentice.

00:07:46.229 --> 00:07:52.270
Simultaneously, FBI Agent Peter Strahm and
his partner Lindsay Perez follow Rigg's trail.

00:07:52.270 --> 00:07:55.089
Perez is injured at the scene of Morgan's
test.

00:07:55.089 --> 00:07:59.960
Strahm then interrogates Jill Tuck, who leads
him to the building John uses for his tests.

00:07:59.960 --> 00:08:03.159
Strahm arrives at John's room just after Jeff
kills John.

00:08:03.159 --> 00:08:05.869
Strahm shoots Jeff in apparent self-defense.

00:08:05.869 --> 00:08:08.099
Hoffman locks Strahm in, but he finds an exit.

00:08:08.099 --> 00:08:11.839
However, he is then captured and put into
the Water Cube trap.

00:08:11.839 --> 00:08:16.319
Strahm barely survives by using a pen to perform
a tracheotomy on himself.

00:08:16.319 --> 00:08:20.800
Hoffman then pretends to escape, and is stunned
to discover Strahm also made it out alive.

00:08:21.800 --> 00:08:25.249
John's autopsy reveals a tape that promises
Hoffman will be tested.

00:08:25.249 --> 00:08:29.400
Hoffman later receives a mysterious note that
warns, "I know who you are."

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:33.430
The note is from Dr. Gordon, who'd received
a tape from Jill's box, in which John asks

00:08:33.430 --> 00:08:35.229
him to watch out for Jill.

00:08:35.229 --> 00:08:39.409
Strahm determines that Hoffman was Jigsaw's
apprentice after reading up on the Seth Baxter

00:08:39.409 --> 00:08:40.409
case.

00:08:40.409 --> 00:08:45.529
Despite being removed from the case by his
superior Dan Erickson, he continues to investigate

00:08:45.529 --> 00:08:46.529
Hoffman.

00:08:46.529 --> 00:08:48.900
Jill complains to Erickson that Strahm is
stalking her.

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:51.959
Meanwhile, Hoffman works to set up Strahm
as a suspect.

00:08:51.959 --> 00:08:56.990
He stages a group trap involving five crooked
people connected to a deadly apartment fire

00:08:56.990 --> 00:08:59.550
Strahm previously investigated.

00:08:59.550 --> 00:09:04.279
Hoffman also uses Strahm's cell phone to lead
Erickson to the location of the group trap.

00:09:04.279 --> 00:09:08.980
Upon finding two victims still alive, Erickson
puts out an APB on Strahm.

00:09:08.980 --> 00:09:12.690
However, Hoffman then leads Strahm to the
Nerve Gas House and traps him in a room that

00:09:12.690 --> 00:09:13.980
crushes him to death.

00:09:14.980 --> 00:09:18.470
Hoffman stages a two-person test so he can
continue framing Strahm.

00:09:18.470 --> 00:09:23.150
Erickson grants Hoffman unfettered access
to the FBI's investigation, and reveals that

00:09:23.150 --> 00:09:26.370
Perez faked her death and is still active
on the case.

00:09:26.370 --> 00:09:31.269
Later, Hoffman carries out Jigsaw's wish for
a test on William Easton, in which Easton

00:09:31.269 --> 00:09:35.220
is forced to make life-or-death decisions
for a series of his employees.

00:09:35.220 --> 00:09:40.029
Finally, the wife and son of the late Harold
Abbott must decide Easton's fate, and they

00:09:40.029 --> 00:09:41.329
choose to kill him.

00:09:41.329 --> 00:09:45.220
Though Jigsaw's work is finally done, Hoffman
is not in the clear.

00:09:45.220 --> 00:09:48.110
Erickson and Perez soon discover Hoffman's
identity.

00:09:48.110 --> 00:09:51.940
As soon as the FBI agents realize who Hoffman
is, however, he kills them.

00:09:52.940 --> 00:09:56.459
The last surprise to come from John's box
for Jill is the Reverse Beartrap.

00:09:56.459 --> 00:09:59.240
John's box instructs Jill to use it on Hoffman.

00:09:59.240 --> 00:10:02.170
However, Hoffman manages to survive the device.

00:10:02.170 --> 00:10:06.421
Hoffman manages to divert police attention
by staging the grisly Horsepower trap, as

00:10:06.421 --> 00:10:11.589
well as the test of Bobby Dagen, who's made
a fortune pretending to be a Jigsaw survivor.

00:10:11.589 --> 00:10:16.220
After setting a deadly trap for Gibson and
other officers, Hoffman manages to sneak himself

00:10:16.220 --> 00:10:20.810
into the body bag of one of the Horsepower
victims to get access to the police station.

00:10:20.810 --> 00:10:24.480
He kills anyone and everyone in his way to
get to Jill's holding cell.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:29.170
Hoffman places Jill in the Reverse Beartrap,
which kills her, and prepares to get away.

00:10:29.170 --> 00:10:32.310
However, he's met outside by three men in
pig masks.

00:10:32.310 --> 00:10:37.029
One of them is Dr. Gordon, who shackles Hoffman
to Adam's old spot in the bathroom and takes

00:10:37.029 --> 00:10:40.160
away the saw that would allow him to save
himself.

00:10:41.160 --> 00:10:44.060
10 years after John Kramer's death, a series
of Jigsaw-like deaths occur.

00:10:44.060 --> 00:10:49.519
The bodies are analyzed by Logan and his strangely
Jigsaw-obsessed assistant Eleanor.

00:10:49.519 --> 00:10:53.230
Detective Halloran is drawn into the case,
but little does he know, he's being set up

00:10:53.230 --> 00:10:54.540
by Logan.

00:10:54.540 --> 00:10:58.790
Halloran is a crooked detective who took a
bribe from the man who murdered Logan's wife.

00:10:58.790 --> 00:11:02.310
The game is a copycat version of the test
Logan survived.

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:07.129
Logan plants puzzle pieces of the new victims
in Halloran's freezer, to make him a suspect.

00:11:07.129 --> 00:11:11.470
Logan then forces Halloran to admit his misdeeds
by pretending to be trapped in a two-person

00:11:11.470 --> 00:11:12.660
test with him.

00:11:12.660 --> 00:11:16.009
After Halloran confesses, Logan reveals that
he has taped him.

00:11:16.009 --> 00:11:22.540
"Innocent people died because of me, I did
it!"

00:11:22.540 --> 00:11:26.980
He watches as Halloran's head is sliced to
pieces in the laser collar trap.

00:11:26.980 --> 00:11:28.139
Game over, for now.

